(lang dune 3.15)

; A NESTED project, not a nested directory: this file is what creates the
; boundary. Dune scopes a library with no public_name to its project, so the
; stanza below is what makes `rivet_tools` invisible to asm/ and asm/'s
; private libraries - lib/, targets/, driver/, vendor/fmt - invisible here.
;
; That isolation is load-bearing rather than tidy. Bos requires the opam `fmt`,
; and vendor/fmt defines a private library of the same name; in one project
; dune rejects the closure outright ("Conflict between the following libraries").
; See docs/design.md.
;
; Deliberately NOT inherited from dune-project: melange (the tools never
; build to JS), menhir, and cram. The lang version matches on purpose - a lower
; one would silently change stanza defaults across the boundary.
;
; There is no .ocamlformat here either: .ocamlformat governs this tree, and
; `dune build @fmt` from asm/ covers it.

; The tools' own package, so that another project can build its command line on
; top of this one: rivet-tools.lib is the fixture, manifest and oracle library,
; rivet-tools.cli the command tree with a pluggable compiler.

(package
 (name rivet-tools)
 (synopsis "Fixture generation, oracle and manifest tooling for rivet"))
